{%- comment -%}
  Seoul Glow Lab — Phoenix Form & Scale (§06 of Phoenix PDP)
  Editorial form study. 2-col on desktop (figure left, copy right) →
  1-col stacked on mobile. The figure stage holds either:
    (a) an inline-Liquid SVG of the lamp profile with dimension labels
        and 5 fan-out arm tips colored by --film-* tokens, OR
    (b) a merchant-uploaded image (use_svg=false fallback).

  Right column = H3 + 2 body paragraphs + hairline + 4-cell metric grid.

  Surface: Paper. Brand-book v1 — H2 italic-gradient `<em>` accent.
  No JS.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign film_gold   = s.film_gold   | default: '#E95F77'
  assign film_amber  = s.film_amber  | default: '#2FA66F'
  assign film_blush  = s.film_blush  | default: '#315BCF'
  assign film_red    = s.film_red    | default: '#28BFC7'
  assign film_violet = s.film_violet | default: '#7A4DCE'
  assign films_str   = film_gold | append: ',' | append: film_amber | append: ',' | append: film_blush | append: ',' | append: film_red | append: ',' | append: film_violet
  assign films       = films_str | split: ','
-%}

<section
  id="casa-form-{{ section.id }}"
  class="casa-form"
  style="
    --pt: {{ s.padding_top    | default: 96 }}px;
    --pb: {{ s.padding_bottom | default: 96 }}px;
    --paper: {{ s.color_paper | default: '#FAFAF7' }};
    --ink:   {{ s.color_ink   | default: '#0A0A0F' }};
    --film-gold:   {{ s.film_gold   | default: '#E95F77' }};
    --film-amber:  {{ s.film_amber  | default: '#2FA66F' }};
    --film-blush:  {{ s.film_blush  | default: '#315BCF' }};
    --film-red:    {{ s.film_red    | default: '#28BFC7' }};
    --film-violet: {{ s.film_violet | default: '#7A4DCE' }};
  "
>
  <header class="casa-form__head">
    {%- if s.kicker != blank -%}
      <p class="casa-form__mono">{{ s.kicker }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="casa-form__h2">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if s.lede != blank -%}
      <p class="casa-form__lede">{{ s.lede }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </header>

  <div class="casa-form__stage">
    <div class="casa-form__figure">
      {%- if s.use_svg -%}
        <svg
          viewBox="0 0 1200 1200"
          class="casa-form__svg"
          preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Phoenix Floor Lamp — chrome pole with five articulating arms and circular sunset-film light heads on a 7.9 × 3 in square base, total height 70.9 in / 180 cm"
        >
          <defs>
            {%- comment -%} Chrome cylinder gradient — used by pole + arm tubes + base {%- endcomment -%}
            <linearGradient id="casa-form-chrome-{{ section.id }}" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="0%">
              <stop offset="0%"   stop-color="#4a4a54"></stop>
              <stop offset="35%"  stop-color="#b8b8c4"></stop>
              <stop offset="50%"  stop-color="#e8e8f0"></stop>
              <stop offset="65%"  stop-color="#b8b8c4"></stop>
              <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#4a4a54"></stop>
            </linearGradient>
            {%- comment -%}
              Wall vignette + floor shadow gradients deleted per merchant
              2026-05-18 15th pass: "The image itself should blend into
              the background. There shouldn't be a box that captures the
              Phoenix lamp... should just sit on the background and emit
              the light." All ambient wash now lives at the SECTION level
              (see .casa-form background in the stylesheet block); the
              SVG is transparent except where the lamp + per-disc glows
              + dimension callouts paint. With no figure box and no SVG
              backdrop, the section's sunset gradient flows behind the
              lamp continuously, with the disc glows adding local hot-
              spots that radiate into the section wash. The floor shadow
              also went away — there is no floor anymore, just sunset.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- comment -%} Gaussian blur for the soft disc halos {%- endcomment -%}
            <filter id="casa-form-disc-glow-{{ section.id }}" x="-100%" y="-100%" width="300%" height="300%">
              <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="8"></feGaussianBlur>
            </filter>
            {%- comment -%}
              Per-arm wall-light radial gradients (one per film color).
              Stops shaped so each disc's light falls off naturally over a
              very long range — hot at the source, soft mid-field, faint
              tail that reaches the far corners (merchant 2026-05-18 14th
              pass: "light gradient... should extend throughout the whole
              image... strong at source and decreases as you move further
              away, but it should move infinitely further away throughout
              the whole image. Sunset vibes, strong, elegant, Apple look").
              The circle these gradients paint into was bumped from r=260
              to r=1000 below so the visible light actually reaches the
              edges. At r=1000 the stops translate to: 5% = 50px (hot
              core just past the 13px disc rim), 16% = 160px (strong
              halo), 38% = 380px (mid-field), 100% = 1000px (long faint
              tail). Screen blend below combines all 5 plus the ambient
              wall wash into one unified sunset gradient.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for i in (0..4) -%}
              <radialGradient id="casa-form-glow-{{ section.id }}-{{ i }}" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
                <stop offset="0%"   stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0.88"></stop>
                <stop offset="5%"   stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0.58"></stop>
                <stop offset="16%"  stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0.30"></stop>
                <stop offset="38%"  stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0.10"></stop>
                <stop offset="70%"  stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0.025"></stop>
                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
              </radialGradient>
            {%- endfor -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Per-disc film gradients — replace the previous flat film
              fill (single hex at opacity 0.92) which read as cartoonish
              colored dots. A real lit gel filter has a hot near-white
              center where the LED emitter is brightest, fading through
              the saturated film color toward a slightly darker rim where
              the housing shadows the edge of the acrylic. Three-stop
              radial gradient at 50%, 50% reproduces that.
              cx=42% cy=38% offsets the highlight up-and-left a touch so
              the disc reads as a 3D dome catching ambient light rather
              than a flat 2D coin. Stop 0 is warm-white (255,250,235)
              instead of pure white — matches the actual color
              temperature of the films when lit.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for i in (0..4) -%}
              <radialGradient id="casa-form-film-{{ section.id }}-{{ i }}" cx="42%" cy="38%" r="62%">
                <stop offset="0%"   stop-color="rgba(255,250,235,0.95)"></stop>
                <stop offset="22%"  stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0.95"></stop>
                <stop offset="78%"  stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0.92"></stop>
                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="{{ films[i] }}" stop-opacity="0.70"></stop>
              </radialGradient>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </defs>

          {%- comment -%}
            Dark wall + ambient wall vignette rects deleted per merchant
            2026-05-18 15th pass ("there shouldn't be a box that captures
            the Phoenix lamp"). The SVG canvas is now fully transparent
            in this band — the section's sunset gradient background
            shows through everywhere outside the lamp shapes + glows.
          {%- endcomment -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Five per-disc glows. Now alpha-composite over a TRANSPARENT
            SVG backdrop (no more dark wall rect) — they paint the
            section's sunset background with their film colors at the
            disc positions, producing the "light emitting FROM the lamp"
            effect the merchant asked for. Each glow uses r=700 — large
            enough to bleed into the section's ambient wash, small
            enough that the lamp reads as the emission source (not a
            generic full-frame wash). The mix-blend-mode: screen still
            applies between overlapping glow circles inside the SVG,
            keeping the multi-color blend natural where two discs
            overlap. The compound SVG-to-section composite then
            alpha-blends onto the section's sunset gradient.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <g style="mix-blend-mode: screen;" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="672" cy="334" r="700" fill="url(#casa-form-glow-{{ section.id }}-0)"></circle>
            <circle cx="528" cy="409" r="700" fill="url(#casa-form-glow-{{ section.id }}-1)"></circle>
            <circle cx="672" cy="484" r="700" fill="url(#casa-form-glow-{{ section.id }}-2)"></circle>
            <circle cx="528" cy="559" r="700" fill="url(#casa-form-glow-{{ section.id }}-3)"></circle>
            <circle cx="672" cy="634" r="700" fill="url(#casa-form-glow-{{ section.id }}-4)"></circle>
          </g>

          {%- comment -%}
            Floor-contact shadow deleted (merchant 2026-05-18 15th pass).
            There is no floor anymore — the lamp sits in a sunset, not
            on a surface. Adding a contact shadow would re-imply the
            "box" we just deleted.
          {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} Chrome pole — 8px wide (matches §04 showcase lamp), full height y=320 to y=986 (top of base) {%- endcomment -%}
          <rect x="596" y="320" width="8" height="666" fill="url(#casa-form-chrome-{{ section.id }})" aria-hidden="true"></rect>
          <rect x="599.4" y="320" width="1" height="666" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.6)" aria-hidden="true"></rect>

          {%- comment -%} Square chrome plinth base — 44 × 14 (matches the 7.9 × 3 in proportion) {%- endcomment -%}
          <rect x="578" y="986" width="44" height="14" fill="url(#casa-form-chrome-{{ section.id }})" aria-hidden="true"></rect>
          <rect x="578" y="986" width="44" height="1.5" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.7)" aria-hidden="true"></rect>
          <rect x="578" y="998.5" width="44" height="1.5" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.55)" aria-hidden="true"></rect>

          {%- comment -%}
            Five arm assemblies — anchors clustered y=390..690 at 75px spacing (top of cluster
            just below pole top, bottom of cluster ~mid-pole). i=0,2,4 right side; i=1,3 left.
            Each arm: bracket clamp + chrome arm tube (vertical rise → quarter-arc → horizontal)
            + diffuser disc (soft halo + housing + film face + LED hot-spot) + power cord.
            All elements per arm use the film color at index `i` from the films array.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign anchors = '390,465,540,615,690' | split: ',' -%}
          {%- for i in (0..4) -%}
            {%- assign anchor_y = anchors[i] | times: 1 -%}
            {%- assign side_modulo = i | modulo: 2 -%}
            {%- if side_modulo == 0 -%}
              {%- assign br_x = 600 -%}
              {%- assign tube_in_x = 607 -%}
              {%- assign tube_out_x = 632 -%}
              {%- assign disc_cx = 672 -%}
              {%- assign cord_ctrl_x = 614 -%}
              {%- assign cord_clip_x = 600 -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign br_x = 586 -%}
              {%- assign tube_in_x = 593 -%}
              {%- assign tube_out_x = 568 -%}
              {%- assign disc_cx = 528 -%}
              {%- assign cord_ctrl_x = 586 -%}
              {%- assign cord_clip_x = 596 -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign curve_y = anchor_y | minus: 30 -%}
            {%- assign tube_top_y = anchor_y | minus: 56 -%}
            {%- assign br_y = anchor_y | minus: 5 -%}
            {%- assign cord_y_start = anchor_y | plus: 5 -%}
            {%- assign cord_y_ctrl = anchor_y | plus: 24 -%}
            {%- assign cord_y_end = anchor_y | plus: 28 -%}
            {%- assign cord_clip_y = anchor_y | plus: 25 -%}
            {%- assign disc_rim_left = disc_cx | minus: 12 -%}

            <g class="casa-form__arm" data-film-index="{{ i }}" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- comment -%} Bracket clamp where arm meets pole {%- endcomment -%}
              <rect x="{{ br_x }}" y="{{ br_y }}" width="14" height="10" fill="#1a1620" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.18)" stroke-width="0.5"></rect>
              <rect x="{{ br_x }}" y="{{ br_y }}" width="14" height="1.2" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.25)"></rect>

              {%- comment -%} Chrome arm tube — rise + quarter-arc + horizontal to disc {%- endcomment -%}
              <path d="M {{ tube_in_x }} {{ br_y }} L {{ tube_in_x }} {{ curve_y }} Q {{ tube_in_x }} {{ tube_top_y }}, {{ tube_out_x }} {{ tube_top_y }} L {{ disc_rim_left }} {{ tube_top_y }}"
                    stroke="url(#casa-form-chrome-{{ section.id }})" stroke-width="4.4" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
              <path d="M {{ tube_in_x }} {{ br_y }} L {{ tube_in_x }} {{ curve_y }} Q {{ tube_in_x }} {{ tube_top_y }}, {{ tube_out_x }} {{ tube_top_y }} L {{ disc_rim_left }} {{ tube_top_y }}"
                    stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.55)" stroke-width="0.9" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>

              {%- comment -%}
                Disc head — minimalistic real-product look (merchant 17th
                pass: "the head of each lamp looks fake and not realistic,
                too cartoonish. Its supposed to have a minimalistic sleek
                look and look exactly like what the head of the lamp looks
                like in real life"). Stripped the previous "lit gel face"
                stack (warm-white center gradient, top-arc highlight, inner
                rim) which read as a cartoon illustration of an emitting
                lens. Real Phoenix discs viewed from the side are simply
                a dark housing with a thin chrome rim — the light is
                visible only as the wall bloom behind them. So that's
                what we draw now:
                  1. r=22 soft per-film wall halo (smaller than before,
                     so it doesn't bleed past the disc edge and look
                     like a glowing aura around the housing itself)
                  2. r=8.5 dark housing fill (#08070c, slightly cooler
                     than the previous #0e0c12 so it reads neutrally
                     against any film color behind it)
                  3. r=8.5 thin chrome rim (rgba 220,222,228 at 0.58
                     alpha, 0.7px stroke) — the only "metal" on the
                     disc, exactly what you see on the product photos
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Diffuser head — ported from the §04 arms-showcase lamp so the
                dimension diagram is a visual REPLICA of the showcase lamp
                (merchant 2026-07-16). Instead of the old flat dark disc, the
                head is a sleek chrome SAUCER BEZEL holding a LIT GLASS FILM
                FACE (bright warm-white centre → saturated film colour), with
                a tiny LED hot-spot and a top specular highlight — the
                dimensional, "lit from within" look the showcase heads have.
                  1. soft per-film bloom (r=32) behind the head
                  2. chrome bezel ellipse rx18 ry14 + hairline shadow
                  3. glass film face ellipse rx14 ry10.5 (lit radial gradient)
                     + edge shadow ring
                  4. LED hot-spot r=2
                  5. top specular ellipse — sells the polished glass dome
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <circle cx="{{ disc_cx }}" cy="{{ tube_top_y }}" r="32" fill="{{ films[i] }}" opacity="0.5" filter="url(#casa-form-disc-glow-{{ section.id }})"></circle>
              <ellipse cx="{{ disc_cx }}" cy="{{ tube_top_y }}" rx="18" ry="14" fill="url(#casa-form-chrome-{{ section.id }})"></ellipse>
              <ellipse cx="{{ disc_cx }}" cy="{{ tube_top_y }}" rx="18" ry="14" fill="none" stroke="rgba(0,0,0,0.45)" stroke-width="0.6"></ellipse>
              <ellipse cx="{{ disc_cx }}" cy="{{ tube_top_y }}" rx="14" ry="10.5" fill="url(#casa-form-film-{{ section.id }}-{{ i }})"></ellipse>
              <ellipse cx="{{ disc_cx }}" cy="{{ tube_top_y }}" rx="14" ry="10.5" fill="none" stroke="rgba(0,0,0,0.32)" stroke-width="0.5"></ellipse>
              <circle cx="{{ disc_cx }}" cy="{{ tube_top_y | minus: 1 }}" r="2" fill="rgba(255,250,240,0.9)"></circle>
              <ellipse cx="{{ disc_cx }}" cy="{{ tube_top_y | minus: 11 }}" rx="7" ry="1.4" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.55)"></ellipse>

              {%- comment -%} Power cord — thin black J-curve drooping from bracket back to pole tab {%- endcomment -%}
              <path d="M {{ tube_in_x }} {{ cord_y_start }} Q {{ cord_ctrl_x }} {{ cord_y_ctrl }}, {{ cord_clip_x }} {{ cord_y_end }}"
                    stroke="#0a080d" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
              <rect x="{{ cord_clip_x }}" y="{{ cord_clip_y }}" width="4" height="6" fill="#1a1620"></rect>
            </g>
          {%- endfor -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Engineering dimensions — overlaid in white/light gray on the dark backdrop.
            70.9 in vertical bracket on the right (spans pole top → base bottom).
            7.9 in horizontal bracket below the base plinth.
            3 in vertical bracket beside the base, measuring its 14-unit thickness.
          {%- endcomment -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Engineering dimensions — cleaned up per merchant 2026-05-18
            11th pass ("some lines don't make sense. The horizontal line
            that extends from the base towards the height of the base
            and at the top doesn't make sense"). All three dimensions
            now use clean callout style — a single measurement line +
            endpoint dots + label, with NO leader lines extending from
            the object out to the dimension line. The bracket sits just
            beside the lamp so the connection is visually implied.
          {%- endcomment -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            70.9 in / 180 cm — single vertical line at x=960 (close to the
            glow's rightmost extent x=932 but inside the viewBox). Was
            x=1080 with two long horizontal leaders that stretched 460+
            units from the lamp. Now just the vertical + end dots.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Ruler pulled in x=960 → 810 (2026-07-04 v2 pass): at 960 the
            line floated ~290 units from the pole and read as disconnected
            chrome in the negative space. 810 keeps ~115 units of clear
            gap from the disc rim (672+22) while visually belonging to
            the lamp.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <line class="casa-form__dim-line" x1="810" y1="320" x2="810" y2="1000" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.85)" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"></line>
          <circle class="casa-form__dim-dot" cx="810" cy="320"  r="6" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.95)" aria-hidden="true"></circle>
          <circle class="casa-form__dim-dot" cx="810" cy="1000" r="6" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.95)" aria-hidden="true"></circle>
          {%- comment -%}
            Label sizes are in viewBox units, so they shrink with the diagram.
            At the old 32/16 the height pair rendered 16px / 8px on a 1920x870
            desktop — the metric line was effectively unreadable (merchant
            2026-07-21: "the lamps are incredibly small, especially the
            measurements"). Roughly doubled so they render ~29px / ~16px.
            The height pair sits to the RIGHT of the lamp, so growing it costs
            no vertical space; the base pairs below are grown less because they
            push toward the spec copy (measured 11px clearance).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <text class="casa-form__dim-major" x="836" y="648" text-anchor="start" font-size="52" font-family="'Inter Casa', 'Inter Fallback', sans-serif" font-weight="800" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.98)" letter-spacing="-0.015em">70.9 in.</text>
          <text class="casa-form__dim-sub" x="837" y="694" text-anchor="start" font-size="28" font-family="'Inter Casa', 'Inter Fallback', sans-serif" font-weight="400" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.75)">180 cm</text>

          {%- comment -%}
            7.9 in / 20 cm — single horizontal line directly below the
            plinth. Brought 20 units closer (y=1040 → y=1020) so the
            bracket sits right under the base, no longer floating low.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <line class="casa-form__dim-line" x1="578" y1="1020" x2="622" y2="1020" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.85)" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"></line>
          <circle class="casa-form__dim-dot" cx="578" cy="1020" r="5" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.95)" aria-hidden="true"></circle>
          <circle class="casa-form__dim-dot" cx="622" cy="1020" r="5" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.95)" aria-hidden="true"></circle>
          <text class="casa-form__dim-major" x="600" y="1066" text-anchor="middle" font-size="34" font-family="'Inter Casa', 'Inter Fallback', sans-serif" font-weight="800" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.98)" letter-spacing="-0.015em">7.9 in.</text>
          <text class="casa-form__dim-sub" x="600" y="1100" text-anchor="middle" font-size="21" font-family="'Inter Casa', 'Inter Fallback', sans-serif" font-weight="400" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.75)">20 cm</text>

          {%- comment -%}
            3 in / 7.6 cm — JUST a vertical line showing the plinth's
            thickness (merchant: "the 3 in is just supposed to be a
            vertical line showing the thickness of the base"). Previous
            bracket had two 38-unit horizontal terminators extending
            from the plinth edge — dropped. Vertical now at x=640
            (18 units right of the plinth's right edge), spans the
            plinth's exact y range (986 → 1000), label beside.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <line class="casa-form__dim-line" x1="640" y1="986" x2="640" y2="1000" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.85)" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"></line>
          <circle class="casa-form__dim-dot" cx="640" cy="986"  r="4" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.95)" aria-hidden="true"></circle>
          <circle class="casa-form__dim-dot" cx="640" cy="1000" r="4" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.95)" aria-hidden="true"></circle>
          <text class="casa-form__dim-major" x="666" y="991"  text-anchor="start" font-size="30" font-family="'Inter Casa', 'Inter Fallback', sans-serif" font-weight="800" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.98)" letter-spacing="-0.015em">3 in.</text>
          <text class="casa-form__dim-sub" x="666" y="1022" text-anchor="start" font-size="19" font-family="'Inter Casa', 'Inter Fallback', sans-serif" font-weight="400" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.75)">7.6 cm</text>
        </svg>
      {%- elsif s.figure_image != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Image mode with dimension callouts overlaid (merchant 2026-05-18
          19th pass — "Replace that Phoenix lamp with this one in the
          screenshot and add all the measurements and heights and
          specifications exactly").

          The wrapper `casa-form__photo-stack` is position:relative so
          the dimension callout divs can absolute-position over the
          image with percent coords (works for any portrait lamp shot).
          mix-blend-mode: lighten on the image lets the section's sunset
          gradient show through dark areas — minimizes the "boxed lamp"
          effect if the uploaded image has its own gradient backdrop.
          For the cleanest result, upload a TRANSPARENT-background PNG
          (lamp only, no backdrop) so the section gradient flows behind
          the lamp seamlessly.

          Dimension positions are tuned for a portrait lamp shot with
          the lamp centered, pole spanning ~5%-88% of image height, and
          a base disc at the bottom ~88-95%. Each label sits OUTSIDE
          the lamp silhouette so it doesn't cover the product:
            70.9 in / 180 cm — vertical bracket on RIGHT, full pole height
            7.9 in  / 20 cm  — horizontal bracket BELOW the base
            3 in    / 7.6 cm — vertical bracket BESIDE the base
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign img_400  = s.figure_image | image_url: width: 400 -%}
        {%- assign img_800  = s.figure_image | image_url: width: 800 -%}
        {%- assign img_1200 = s.figure_image | image_url: width: 1200 -%}
        {%- assign img_1600 = s.figure_image | image_url: width: 1600 -%}
        <div class="casa-form__photo-stack">
          <picture class="casa-form__pic">
            <img
              srcset="{{ img_400 }} 400w, {{ img_800 }} 800w, {{ img_1200 }} 1200w, {{ img_1600 }} 1600w"
              sizes="(min-width: 1100px) 720px, 100vw"
              src="{{ img_1200 }}"
              alt="{{ s.figure_alt | default: 'Phoenix Floor Lamp — chrome pole with five articulating arms and circular sunset-film light heads on a 7.9 in base, 70.9 in / 180 cm total height' | escape }}"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              width="{{ s.figure_image.width }}"
              height="{{ s.figure_image.height }}"
            >
          </picture>

          {%- comment -%} 70.9 in / 180 cm — vertical bracket on the right side {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="casa-form__dim casa-form__dim--height" aria-label="Total height 70.9 inches / 180 centimeters">
            <span class="casa-form__dim-bar"></span>
            <span class="casa-form__dim-label">
              <span class="casa-form__dim-major">70.9 in.</span>
              <span class="casa-form__dim-sub">180 cm</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%} 7.9 in / 20 cm — horizontal bracket below the base {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="casa-form__dim casa-form__dim--width" aria-label="Base width 7.9 inches / 20 centimeters">
            <span class="casa-form__dim-bar"></span>
            <span class="casa-form__dim-label">
              <span class="casa-form__dim-major">7.9 in.</span>
              <span class="casa-form__dim-sub">20 cm</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%} 3 in / 7.6 cm — small vertical bracket beside the base {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="casa-form__dim casa-form__dim--depth" aria-label="Base depth 3 inches / 7.6 centimeters">
            <span class="casa-form__dim-bar"></span>
            <span class="casa-form__dim-label">
              <span class="casa-form__dim-major">3 in.</span>
              <span class="casa-form__dim-sub">7.6 cm</span>
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Default fallback — Phoenix dimensional drawing from the product's media gallery
          (file `3_in._copy.webp` in Shopify Files). Used when use_svg is off AND no
          merchant-uploaded figure_image is set. Hardcoded so the section "just works"
          for Phoenix without the merchant having to re-pick the image.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign dim_base = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0442/0691/5738/files/3_in._copy.webp' -%}
        <picture class="casa-form__pic">
          <img
            srcset="{{ dim_base }}?width=400 400w, {{ dim_base }}?width=800 800w, {{ dim_base }}?width=1200 1200w, {{ dim_base }}?width=1600 1600w"
            sizes="(min-width: 1100px) 480px, 100vw"
            src="{{ dim_base }}?width=800"
            alt="Phoenix Floor Lamp dimensional drawing — 70.9 in / 180 cm total height, 7.9 in / 20 cm base width, 3 in / 7.6 cm base depth"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            width="2000"
            height="2000"
          >
        </picture>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="casa-form__copy">
      {%- if s.h3 != blank -%}
        <h3 class="casa-form__h3">{{ s.h3 }}</h3>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if s.body_1 != blank -%}
        <div class="casa-form__body">{{ s.body_1 }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if s.body_2 != blank -%}
        <div class="casa-form__body">{{ s.body_2 }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="casa-form__meta">
        {%- assign metric_ids = '1,2,3,4' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- for n in metric_ids -%}
          {%- assign val_key = 'metric_' | append: n | append: '_value' -%}
          {%- assign lbl_key = 'metric_' | append: n | append: '_label' -%}
          {%- assign val = s[val_key] -%}
          {%- assign lbl = s[lbl_key] -%}
          {%- if val != blank or lbl != blank -%}
            <div class="casa-form__metric">
              {%- if val != blank -%}<strong>{{ val }}</strong>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if lbl != blank -%}<em>{{ lbl }}</em>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  .casa-form {
    /* Section is one big sunset gradient (merchant 16th pass: "the
       gradient should flow throughout the whole of this section and
       into the section above it and below it. It shouldn't look like
       anything's being cut off").

       Strategy: drop the previous top/bottom linear-feather-to-ink
       (which was creating a visible dark band at the section seams).
       Instead, anchor the radial sunset wash at 50% center with a low-
       opacity tail that reaches the corners, and use #0A0A0F as the
       base color — same ink as §05 above and the FAQ below. With both
       sections terminating in #0A0A0F and the sunset wash fading to
       transparent at the edges, the seam is invisible and the wash
       reads as continuous between sections.

       Radial wash extended both horizontally (78% → 95%) and vertically
       (62% → 92%) so even the section corners pick up faint sunset
       color before falling to the base ink. */
    background:
      /* Top + bottom feather to PURE INK with a 3-stop ease curve so
         the dark→sunset transition reads as a smooth gradient, not a
         visible band. Matches the recipe on §04 + §05 (Phoenix mood)
         so every section edge meets at identical #0A0A0F across the
         whole §02→§06 stack (merchant 2026-05-18 17th pass: "doesn't
         flow seamlessly into each other... no break-offs or cut-offs").
         Combined with the wider radial wash below (95%×92% per the
         upstream merchant work that ran in parallel), the result is:
         (a) corners + edges of section are pure #0A0A0F via feather,
         (b) inner ~56% of section height shows the rich sunset wash,
         (c) section boundaries at top/bottom meet adjacent §05/§07
             at identical pixel values — seams invisible. */
      linear-gradient(180deg,
        #0A0A0F 0%,
        rgba(10, 10, 15, 0.86) 6%,
        rgba(10, 10, 15, 0.40) 14%,
        rgba(10, 10, 15, 0) 22%,
        rgba(10, 10, 15, 0) 78%,
        rgba(10, 10, 15, 0.40) 86%,
        rgba(10, 10, 15, 0.86) 94%,
        #0A0A0F 100%
      ),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 95% 92% at 50% 50%,
        rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.36) 0%,
        rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.24) 28%,
        rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.16) 58%,
        rgba(30, 16, 40, 0.06) 85%,
        rgba(10, 10, 15, 0) 100%
      ),
      #0A0A0F;
    color: #FAFAF7;
    /* Horizontal padding tightened clamp(20,5vw,64) → clamp(16,2.5vw,32)
       so the stage can fill more of the viewport at 1440. */
    padding: var(--pt, 96px) clamp(16px, 2.5vw, 32px) var(--pb, 96px);
    font-family: var(--font-body--family, "Inter", system-ui, sans-serif);
  }
  .casa-form__head {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    /* Kicker + H2 + lede center-aligned per merchant 2026-05-18 12th
       pass ("the text and the images must be center aligned as well as
       the title"). Was left-aligned text inside a centered block. */
    text-align: center;
  }
  .casa-form__lede {
    /* Center the lede block + cap its width — was inheriting head's
       flex-start alignment which left it pinned to one side. */
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .casa-form__mono {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(250, 250, 247, 0.62);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .casa-form__h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family, "Inter", system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .casa-form__h2 em {
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .casa-form__lede {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: rgba(250, 250, 247, 0.82);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .casa-form__stage {
    /* Single-centerline stack (merchant 2026-05-18 12th pass: "the text
       and the images must be center aligned as well as the title").
       Was a 2-col grid (figure | copy) — now a single column with the
       figure centered above the copy. Same pattern as §02 carousel.
       Title is already centered above the stage. */
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 56px);
  }

  .casa-form__figure {
    /* Centerpiece. Background NUKED per merchant 2026-05-18 15th pass
       ("the image itself should blend into the background. There
       shouldn't be a box that captures the Phoenix lamp"). The figure
       is now a transparent slot — the section's sunset gradient flows
       continuously behind the lamp. Overflow stays visible so the disc
       glows (r=700 inside the SVG) can bleed past the figure rectangle
       into the surrounding section if needed; the SVG itself still
       paints inside its own viewBox, so this is harmless either way.
       aspect-ratio 1/1 preserved so the layout doesn't shift. */
    width: 100%;
    max-width: clamp(640px, 70vw, 920px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: transparent;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    overflow: visible;
  }
  .casa-form__svg,
  .casa-form__pic img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: block;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  /* ── Image-with-dimensions overlay (when figure_image is set) ─────
     The photo-stack wraps the picture + 3 dimension callouts so the
     callouts position absolutely over the lamp image. Percent coords
     tuned for a portrait lamp shot — pole spans ~5%-88%, base disc
     sits at bottom ~88-93%. Dimension labels sit OUTSIDE the lamp
     silhouette so they don't cover the product (merchant Rule 1).
     mix-blend-mode: lighten on the image lets the section's sunset
     gradient bleed through dark pixels — softens the box-effect if
     the uploaded image has its own backdrop. For seamless flow,
     upload a transparent-background PNG.                              */
  .casa-form__photo-stack {
    /* height: auto + aspect-ratio: inherit down the whole stack→pic→img
       chain instead of height: 100% — the figure's height comes from its
       own aspect-ratio (1/1), and Safari 26 can fail to resolve a %-height
       against that (the /cart flat-thumbnail class; immune pattern from
       .cart-items__media-image in snippets/cart-products.liquid). The
       stack's width equals the figure's width, so the inherited ratio
       resolves each box to the same square; the %-coord dimension
       callouts keep the same reference box. */
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: inherit;
  }
  .casa-form__photo-stack .casa-form__pic {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: inherit;
    display: block;
  }
  .casa-form__photo-stack .casa-form__pic img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: inherit;
    object-fit: contain;
    display: block;
    mix-blend-mode: lighten;
  }

  .casa-form__dim {
    position: absolute;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .casa-form__dim-bar {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    display: block;
    position: relative;
  }
  /* Endpoint dots on the bracket. Pseudo-elements so we don't add DOM. */
  .casa-form__dim-bar::before,
  .casa-form__dim-bar::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 100px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
  }
  .casa-form__dim-label {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .casa-form__dim-label .casa-form__dim-major {
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: clamp(14px, 1.2vw, 18px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
  }
  .casa-form__dim-label .casa-form__dim-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: clamp(11px, 0.85vw, 13px);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
  }

  /* 70.9 in / 180 cm — vertical bracket on right side, full lamp height. */
  .casa-form__dim--height {
    top: 5%;
    bottom: 8%;
    right: 6%;
    flex-direction: row;
  }
  .casa-form__dim--height .casa-form__dim-bar {
    width: 2px;
    height: 100%;
  }
  .casa-form__dim--height .casa-form__dim-bar::before { top: -5px; left: -4px; }
  .casa-form__dim--height .casa-form__dim-bar::after  { bottom: -5px; left: -4px; }
  .casa-form__dim--height .casa-form__dim-label {
    align-self: center;
    margin-left: 12px;
  }

  /* 7.9 in / 20 cm — horizontal bracket below the base, centered. */
  .casa-form__dim--width {
    left: 42%;
    right: 42%;
    bottom: 3%;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .casa-form__dim--width .casa-form__dim-bar {
    height: 2px;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .casa-form__dim--width .casa-form__dim-bar::before { left: -5px; top: -4px; }
  .casa-form__dim--width .casa-form__dim-bar::after  { right: -5px; top: -4px; }
  .casa-form__dim--width .casa-form__dim-label {
    margin-top: 8px;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* 3 in / 7.6 cm — vertical bracket beside base, just outside its right edge. */
  .casa-form__dim--depth {
    right: 32%;
    bottom: 8%;
    height: 6%;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .casa-form__dim--depth .casa-form__dim-bar {
    width: 2px;
    height: 100%;
  }
  .casa-form__dim--depth .casa-form__dim-bar::before { top: -4px; left: -3px; width: 8px; height: 8px; }
  .casa-form__dim--depth .casa-form__dim-bar::after  { bottom: -4px; left: -3px; width: 8px; height: 8px; }
  .casa-form__dim--depth .casa-form__dim-label {
    margin-left: 10px;
  }

  .casa-form__copy {
    /* Copy block — centered below the figure (merchant 2026-05-18 12th
       pass). max-width 640px keeps the editorial column readable; text
       inside stays left-aligned (paragraphs read better that way), the
       BLOCK is what's centered horizontally. */
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 22px;
  }
  .casa-form__h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family, "Inter", system-ui, sans-serif);
    /* H3 bumped 22 → clamp(22, 1.8vw, 26) — fluid at desktop, mobile
       still gets its 19px override in the @max-width:749 block below. */
    font-size: clamp(22px, 1.8vw, 26px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 32ch;
  }
  .casa-form__body {
    /* Body bumped 14 → clamp(15, 1.05vw, 16). Color flipped to light-on-
       sunset per 2026-05-18 15th pass (section is no longer paper). */
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.05vw, 16px);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: rgba(250, 250, 247, 0.82);
  }
  .casa-form__body p { margin: 0 0 0.75em; }
  .casa-form__body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .casa-form__meta {
    /* Border colors flipped to light-on-dark per 2026-05-18 15th pass. */
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0;
    margin-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(250, 250, 247, 0.12);
  }
  .casa-form__metric {
    /* Padding bumped 16 → 18 to give the larger stat values room. */
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(250, 250, 247, 0.12);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 5px;
  }
  .casa-form__metric:nth-child(odd) { padding-right: 16px; border-right: 1px solid rgba(250, 250, 247, 0.12); }
  .casa-form__metric:nth-child(even) { padding-left: 16px; }
  .casa-form__metric strong {
    /* Stat values bumped clamp(20,2vw,26) → clamp(26,2.4vw,32). */
    font-size: clamp(26px, 2.4vw, 32px);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1;
    background: linear-gradient(120deg,
      var(--film-gold, #E95F77) 0%,
      var(--film-amber, #2FA66F) 25%,
      var(--film-blush, #315BCF) 50%,
      var(--film-red, #28BFC7) 75%,
      var(--film-violet, #7A4DCE) 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
            background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
            color: transparent;
  }
  .casa-form__metric em {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    /* Stat labels bumped 10 → 11. Color flipped to light-on-dark. */
    font-size: 11px;
    font-style: normal;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(250, 250, 247, 0.62);
  }

  /* Phoenix §05↔§06 seam continuity is now handled by the seam-matched
     master gradient in assets/casa-phoenix.css — §05's bottom and §06's
     top share --phx-seam-4 (burnt orange), so the boundary pixel is
     identical on both sides. The old `:root.is-phoenix .casa-form::before`
     that painted a sunset radial 340px UP past §06's top was a
     compensation for ink-feathered neighbours and introduced its own
     visible edge — removed. Apollo and every other PDP using this
     section keep their original bg unaffected. */

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .casa-form { padding: 64px clamp(20px, 5vw, 32px); }
    .casa-form__h3 { font-size: 19px; }

    /* Dimension labels — mobile size dialed back per merchant 2026-05-18
       16th pass ("features are too big now, they overlap with the cm
       and cover part of the images"). Was 70/44 SVG units at scale 1.42
       → ~22/14px screen, which felt aggressive next to the lamp. Now
       38/24 → ~12/7.5px at base figure size, ~16/10px at the Phoenix
       scale of 1.42. Lamp dominates, labels read as supporting chrome.
       Dot + line widths trimmed to match. Desktop uses the inline SVG
       font-size attributes (22/18/15 majors, 13/11/10 subs). */
    .casa-form__svg .casa-form__dim-major { font-size: 38px; }
    .casa-form__svg .casa-form__dim-sub   { font-size: 24px; }
    .casa-form__svg .casa-form__dim-line  { stroke-width: 2.6; }
    .casa-form__svg .casa-form__dim-dot   { r: 6; }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Casa Form Editorial",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "shopify-section-casa-form-editorial",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Headline"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "kicker",
      "label": "Kicker (mono)"
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Product-specific — enter per template. Pre-2026-05-17 defaulted to Phoenix copy which bled onto other floor lamps."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "lede",
      "label": "Lede"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Figure"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "use_svg",
      "label": "Use inline SVG diagram",
      "info": "When on, renders a Liquid-drawn product profile with dimension callouts. When off, uses the image picker below.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "figure_image",
      "label": "Figure image (fallback)",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.use_svg == false }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "figure_alt",
      "label": "Figure alt text",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.use_svg == false }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Copy"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "h3",
      "label": "H3"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body_1",
      "label": "Body 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body_2",
      "label": "Body 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Metrics (4)"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "metric_1_value", "label": "Metric 1 value", "info": "Product-specific — enter per template (Phoenix/Solara/etc. each have different dims)." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "metric_1_label", "label": "Metric 1 label" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "metric_2_value", "label": "Metric 2 value" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "metric_2_label", "label": "Metric 2 label" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "metric_3_value", "label": "Metric 3 value" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "metric_3_label", "label": "Metric 3 label" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "metric_4_value", "label": "Metric 4 value" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "metric_4_label", "label": "Metric 4 label" },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Film colors (5)"
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "film_gold",   "label": "Rose Ember (pink-red)",             "default": "#E95F77" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "film_amber",  "label": "Emerald Glow (green)",              "default": "#2FA66F" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "film_blush",  "label": "Cobalt Dusk (deep blue)",           "default": "#315BCF" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "film_red",    "label": "Turquoise Horizon (turquoise blue)", "default": "#28BFC7" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "film_violet", "label": "Aurora Fusion (red-blue gradient)",  "default": "#7A4DCE" },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Surface"
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_paper", "label": "Background", "default": "#FAFAF7" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_ink",   "label": "Ink (text)", "default": "#0A0A0F" },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_top",    "label": "Top",    "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 96 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_bottom", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 96 }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Casa Form Editorial" }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
